{"v":"3.0.0","project":{"accession":"PRJNA1426335","title":"Metagenomic sequencing of various municipal and hospital water and biofilm samples","description":"Environmental microbiomes are sources of diverse antibiotic resistance determinants that can be mobilized and transferred to human pathogens under a selection pressure from antibiotics. Hospital sewers contain more antibiotics than most environments and are thus increasingly recognized as potential arenas for resistance evolution. However, it is unknown if resistance selection occurs there and what the drivers are. Here we show selection of antibiotic-resistant bacteria within Swedish hospital sewers. Metagenomic data generated in this study served as evidence of selection among the various types of water and biofilm samples. The data was used to estimate the number of antibiotic resistance gene occurrences in the various samples. Understanding how selection occurs in hospital sewers could help in influencing future management and mitigation strategies to prevent risk of antibiotic resistance evolution and transmission.","organism":null,"data_type":"Raw sequence reads","center_name":"University of Gothenburg","submission_date":"2026/02/20 00:00","last_update":null},"sample_cols":["accession","title","collection_date","country","region","city","lat","lon","urban_status","urban_context","eligibility_reason","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","host","location_resolution","country_iso2","place_id","location_status","location_method","location_note","geo_loc_raw","collection_year"],"samples":[["SAMN55849201","Kungalv Site 1-241107","2024-11-07","Sweden","Västra Götaland","Kungälv",57.8783,11.9695,"probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","city-level location without sample-site confirmation","Hospital Wastewater",null,null,null,null,"coordinate","SE",2698739,"verified","text+coordinates",null,"Sweden:Kungalv",2024],["SAMN55849202","Kungalv Site 1-241003","2024-10-03","Sweden","Västra 